note bottom of App
  Registers route modules directly.
  No AllRoutes class and no routes/index.ts.

  Register raw webhook handling before normal JSON parsing.
  Protected JSON routes:
  context/limits -> JSON parser -> auth/role -> validation -> handler.

  Register 404/error handlers after routes.
  Bind callbacks or use arrow methods to preserve this.
end note

note bottom of DependencyRoot
  Manual constructor injection.
  Compose once per process.

  Build settings/logger/database/adapters/repositories,
  then services, middleware and route dependencies.

  API and worker have independent entry points.
  Shared instances remain stateless.
end note

note bottom of AdminService
  Keep existing /admin paths.
  Delegate to hotel, booking and refund services.

  All management access is scoped to the verified hotel owner.
  No client-provided ownerId or isAdmin boolean grants access.
end note

note bottom of DatabaseClient
  One ORM client and connection pool per process.

  Services own transaction boundaries and pass tx explicitly.
  Never store tx on shared repositories.

  TransactionWork<T> =
  (tx: TransactionContext) => Promise<T>.

  ReadWork/QueryWork are internal repository callbacks.
  Commit on success; rollback on thrown failure.

  ORM for routine queries.
  Parameterized SQL for PostGIS and required locking.

  Provider and email calls stay outside DB transactions.
  Migrations/seeding run as deployment commands.
end note

note bottom of BookingService
  One transaction:
  claim idempotency -> lock offering/room -> expire stale holds
  -> check availability/capacity/price -> insert booking
  -> audit -> save replay outcome.

  Hold: 10 minutes.
  Stay: [checkIn, checkOut), 1..30 nights.
  Maximum advance: 365 days.

  Preserve booking snapshots.
  Cancel and enqueue full-refund intent atomically.
  Confirmed cancellation is before hotel-local check-in date.
end note

note bottom of CaptureProcessor
  Shared by checkout, webhook and reconciliation.

  Verify captured status, account, order, amount and currency.
  Lock booking before applying capture.

  Confirm only unexpired PENDING_PAYMENT at processing time.
  Late capture queues refund.
  Never revive cancelled or expired bookings.

  Unique provider payment ID and booking_applied_at
  prevent duplicate effects.
end note

note bottom of PaymentService
  Commit provider intent before network call.
  Persist provider outcome in another short transaction.

  Unknown outcome requires reconciliation before creation retry.
  Local payment-order UUID is the provider receipt.
  Receipt is not a provider idempotency guarantee.

  VerificationOutcome selects HTTP 200 or 202.
end note

note bottom of WebhookService
  Verify signature on untouched raw bytes before parsing.
  Persist unique event ID and payload hash before acknowledgment.

  Apply effects and mark processed atomically.
  Record unsupported signed events as ignored.
end note

note bottom of RefundService
  Full refunds only in v1.
  One refund intent per payment.

  Call provider outside DB transaction.
  Reconcile unknown outcomes before retrying creation.
  Admin retry cannot bypass successful or unknown state guards.
end note

note bottom of BackgroundWorker
  Separate process from HTTP server.
  Durable PostgreSQL work; no Redis required for v1.

  Hold expiry, email, webhook, payment and refund jobs.

  Stop claiming on shutdown.
  Await bounded in-flight work, then close database pool.
end note

note bottom of Lease
  Database assigns locked_until while claiming work.
  Lease.until is the exact persisted deadline.

  Guard completion/retry using expected locked_until
  and verify the claim remains valid.

  Use database time and consistent lock ordering.
  Leases do not guarantee exactly-once external effects.
end note

note bottom of NotificationService
  Transactional outbox with unique message key.
  Encrypt sensitive reset-email payloads.

  Send outside DB transactions.
  Bounded retries and guarded completion.

  Delivery is at least once:
  a crash after sending can duplicate an email.
end note

note bottom of AuthService
  Customer registration only.
  Owner-management accounts are provisioned separately.

  Create user, audit actor and session atomically.
  Hash passwords and opaque refresh/reset tokens.

  Rotate refresh tokens under lock.
  Preserve token-family absolute expiry.

  Commit reuse-triggered family revocation
  before returning unauthorized.

  Reset password, consume reset token
  and revoke sessions atomically.
end note

note bottom of IdempotencyService
  Unique caller + operation + key.
  Compare normalized request hash.

  Claim, business writes and stored outcome share one transaction.
  Replays receive a fresh timestamp/request_id.

  External operations also require durable provider intents.
end note

note bottom of APIResponse
  Success: status=success, code=2xx, errors=[].
  Error: status=error, code=4xx/5xx, data=null, errors nonempty.

  Body code equals HTTP status.
  Timestamp is UTC ISO 8601.
  request_id is generated by server.

  Lists use data.items and data.pagination.
  Acknowledgments use null data.
end note

note bottom of ValidationSchemas
  Define explicit schemas for every endpoint:
  body, path, query and relevant headers.

  Validate UUIDs, formats, bounds, enums and lengths.
  Parse transport strings deliberately.
  Reject unknown writable fields and empty PATCH bodies.

  Optional means omitted; nullable means explicit null.
  Check city versus coordinates and paired stay dates.
  Services enforce ownership and database-dependent rules.
end note

note bottom of RoomTypeInputDTO
  Current Swagger supplies name.
  Persistence references room_type_master.

  Resolve the master lookup/input mapping before implementation.
  Do not silently create arbitrary master records.
end note

note bottom of bookings
  GiST exclusion prevents room overlap for:
  PENDING_PAYMENT, CONFIRMED and CHECKED_IN.

  Do not use now() in the exclusion predicate.
  Enforce hotel/offering/room consistency with composite FKs.
  total_amount = price_per_night * nights.

  is_active does not bypass inventory or financial integrity.
end note

note bottom of audit_logs
  Append-only.
  updated_at/updated_by remain equal to insert values.
  is_active remains true.

  All created_by and updated_by columns reference audit_actors.id.
  Seed system actor with documented self-FK bootstrap.
end note

legend bottom
  One consolidated v1 diagram.

  Node.js/TypeScript modular monolith.
  PostgreSQL/PostGIS.
  Razorpay TEST.

  44 Swagger operations:
  health 1, auth 6, user 3, hotels 4,
  customer bookings 4, payments/webhook 4,
  customer refunds 1, admin 21.

  Implementations realize all methods on their interfaces.
  DTO/type/enum boxes are contracts, not mandatory runtime classes.

  Filenames are relative to src/.
  Persistence schema: repositories/schema/schema.prisma.
  PostgreSQL-specific constraints also require versioned migrations.

  Public money: safe integer INR paise.
  Database money: BIGINT.
  Convert bigint explicitly; do not serialize it directly.

  UUID = branded string.
  LocalDate = YYYY-MM-DD.
  LocalTime = HH:mm or HH:mm:ss.
  JsonObject/JsonValue = recursive JSON-safe types.

  Framework/runtime types come from Express, Node,
  the selected ORM, validator and logger.

  ADMIN retains Swagger naming but is owner-scoped in v1.
  payment_orders.id replaces the removed correlation_key.
endlegend

@enduml